            <ArticleTitle>Chronic ankle instability and pain: a case report of a teenager with open epiphysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>504-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author discusses the treatment of chronic ankle instability in a young child of 14 years of age. A procedure is described that avoids drilling of the fibula and disruption of the epiphyseal plate. An autogenous graft procedure is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
